From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:23:20 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 37/71] Meridian: updater (GitHub release, SHA256SUMS,
 same-certificate check, swap and relaunch)

A little after start and daily, Meridian asks GitHub for its latest
release; a newer one's zip is downloaded in the background, checked
against the release's SHA256SUMS and against this build's code-signing
requirement, and unpacked. The sidebar then offers "Restart to update":
Meridian quits (the session is saved) and a small script swaps the app
and opens the new one. Run from a disk image or an unwritable folder it
points to the release page. Settings > General shows the version and
Check for Updates. Development (ad-hoc) builds don't update themselves.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
